      "artist": "Tony Atkin",
      "description": "Camellia Woodland. It's an overcast grey February day, raining off and on.  It's in the middle of bare deciduous woodland whose branches and twigs will occasionally release large drops of water onto your head just to remind you that it will rain again soon.  In the middle of this scene these foreign interlopers, camellia bushes, are exploding with a riot of colour.  Here's a close up of one of the flowers from the nearest bush 347687.",
