      "artist": "Tony Atkin",
      "description": "Camellias behind Mount Edgcumbe House. Camellias are an early flowering shrub and the mild weather this winter has brought them out particularly early, unfortunately mild weather is accompanied by strong winds and almost continuous rain which does not help to show off the blooms at their best, however not all the camellias at Mount Edgcumbe are in such an exposed position and there are plenty more to find.  Here are some close up photos of the blossom: 347682, 347685, 347687.",
